{{Quote|Kill anyone they would. Kill the water. Kill the squigglies. Care not a ''snod'' who they kill, ''haye?"<br />[Freedi speaks Narkinian]<br />"''Scob the Empire. They not be killing ye. ''Naye'' today.|Dewi and Freedi Pamular decide not to turn in the fugitives|audio=Dewi-ScobTheEmpire.flac|<ref name="Andor11" />}}
'''Dewi Pamular''' was a [[Keredian]] [[Gender|male]] [[fisher]] who worked on the [[moon]] [[Narkina 5]] with his brother, [[Freedi Pamular]]. While [[fishing]] at a quarry [[Water|lake]] on the moon in around [[5 BBY]], the pair captured [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] and [[Ruescott Melshi]], fugitives who had escaped from a nearby [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|prison]].

Dewi and Freedi discussed turning in the [[prisoner]]s for a [[Currency|reward]], but as the Empire was responsible for spoiling the local waters and [[Death|killing]] off the [[fish]] that the brothers would usually catch, they decided to help Andor and Melshi escape instead, taking them to the [[Planet|world]] [[Niamos]] on board their [[TUG-b13|quadjumper]].

==Biography==
===Fishing in poisoned waters===
{{Quote|Prison done it. Spoiled our water. All our water. ''Haye'', Freedi?''"<br />[Freedi speaks Narkinian]<br />"''No biggy dinner tonight like past times, Freedi?''"<br />[Freedi speaks Narkinian]<br />"Haye''. Water spoil here and far. All your ''scobbin'' prison.|Dewi and Freedi Pamular|audio=Dewi-WaterSpoiled.flac|<ref name="Andor11" />}}
[[File:DewiCaptives-A11.png|thumb|right|300px|alt=On a white sand beach in a gray stone quarry, Dewi Pamular looms over Cassian Andor and Ruescott Melshi, both of who lie on the floor wrapped in sticky netting. In the background Freedi Pamular stands by a large rock.|Dewi and Freedi Pamular captured the escaped Cassian Andor and Ruescott Melshi.]]
Dewi Pamular was a [[Keredian]]<ref name="Trivia2" /> [[Gender|male]] from<ref name="Databank" /> the [[moon]]<ref name="8Audio">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> [[Narkina 5]], where he worked as a [[fisher]], spending much of his [[time]]<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|dewi-pamular|Dewi Pamular}}</ref> on [[fishing]] expeditions<ref name="Freedi">{{Databank|freedi-pamular|Freedi Pamular}}</ref> to the moon's quarry [[Water|pools]] with his brother, [[Freedi Pamular]]. The pair hunted for [[Foodstuff|edible]] [[fish]] in the murky pools,<ref name="Databank" /> but [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[prison]]s built on the moon spoiled the water and [[Death|killed]] off most of the fish.<ref name="Andor11" /> In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{AndorDate|111}}</ref> the pair traveled to a quarry lake on the moon in a [[TUG-b13|quadjumper]] and set up fishing nets and equipment on the edge of the water.<ref name="Andor11" />

As they tended to the nets, the brothers were watched by [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] and [[Ruescott Melshi]], [[human]] escapees from [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|one]] of the prisons, who then rushed down into the quarry and toward the quadjumper, which they hoped to steal. The Pamulars watched the [[prisoner]]s run past without giving chase, and before Melshi and Andor could reach the [[Starship|ship]], they triggered a [[sensor]], causing sticky netting to be fired over the humans and reel them in.<ref name="Andor11" />

===Escape from Narkina 5===
{{Dialogue|Dewi|Wise to be jumping quickly, though. Where ye be looking to run now, eh?|Freedi|line2=no|[Grunts affirmingly]|Andor|Niamos?|Dewi|Oh.|Freedi|Niamos. ''Haye''. Niamos.|Dewi|Oh, yeah.|attr=Dewi and Freedi Pamular and Cassian Andor discuss escaping Narkina 5|src=<ref name="Andor11" />}}
Chuckling, the brothers approached their new captives, with Dewi musing that they could turn in the fugitives for a thousand [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] each. He then complained about the Imperial prisons killing off their catch, prompting Melshi and Andor to claim that they had killed nothing and that it was the Empire who was responsible for the fishermen's woes. Freedi pointed out that the Imperials [[Currency|paid]] for the return of prisoners alive or dead, extending out a blade prosthetic, but Dewi agreed with the prisoners that the Empire was the one causing their problems.<ref name="Andor11" />

[[File:PamularQuadjumper.png|thumb|left|300px|alt=A worn Quadjumper with green plating on top begins to lift off from the white sand in the quarry.|Dewi and Freedi Pamular flew the prisoners to Niamos in their quadjumper.]]
After the prisoners began to plead, Freedi deactivated the sensor and released the humans from the netting as Dewi proclaimed that the Empire would not kill them that [[Local day|day]]. Dewi then suggested that they leave quickly, and Andor explained that they wished to escape to<ref name="Andor11" /> the [[Planet|world]]<ref name="Niamos">{{Databank|niamos|Niamos}}</ref> [[Niamos]].<ref name="Andor11" /> The brothers agreed, and the group successfully departed from Narkina 5 and traveled to Niamos in the quadjumper,<ref name="Episode11Guide">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e11-story-gallery|text="Daughter of Ferrix" Story Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 2}}</ref> where the brothers parted ways with the prisoners.<ref name="Andor11" /> A captioned illustration of Dewi and Freedi was included on a map of Narkina 5 that [[artist]] [[Gammit Chond]] created that was later published by the [[Graf Archive]] in an updated version of the ''[[Galactic Atlas]]'' at some point after the [[Battle of Exegol]] in [[35 ABY]].<ref name="AtlasUpdated">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> 

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Mysie my.''"<br />[Freedi speaks Narkinian]<br />"''Prison, ''haye?'' Escapers. Toosie-two. A thousand each the offer be. One for each of us, Freedi.''"<br />[Freedi speaks Narkinian]|Dewi Pamular spoke in broken Basic|audio=Dewi-TwosieTwo.flac|<ref name="Andor11" />}}
Dewi was a hulking<ref name="Andor11Audio">{{Andor|Daughter of Ferrix}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> Keredian with [[Color|black]] [[hair]] and yellow skin.<ref name="Andor11" /> He was the chattier of the two brothers,<ref name="Databank" /> who were not [[blood]] relatives,<ref name="Trivia2" /> and spoke [[Narkinian]] with Freedi but could also speak broken [[Galactic Basic Standard|Basic]], referring to fish as "squigglies."<ref name="Andor11" /> He had compassion<ref name="Databank" /> for those like Andor and Melshi<ref name="Andor11" /> who had been scarred by the Empire, as he had no love for the Imperials who had [[poison]]ed his home which hurt him and his brother's livelihood by killing the fish.<ref name="Databank" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|Better fishing on land these times, ''haye?''<nowiki />|Dewi Pamular|audio=Dewi-BetterFishing.flac|<ref name="Andor11" />}}
Dewi wore brown [[Clothing|pants]], a brown shirt, a green shawl, gray [[boot]]s, and a gray [[hat]]. The Keredian had a [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] [[eye]]. While fishing, Dewi used nets and other equipment and traveled in a quadjumper, which was protected by a sensor and sticky,<ref name="Andor11" /> organic netting.<ref name="Andor11Audio" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|The most successful creatures I wrote were in season one when they escaped from Narkina 5, and then Cassian and Melshi see the two fisherman. I wrote this whole alien language for them, and they’re so great. People were like, "If you can do that, why aren't you doing more of it?" But it was a lot of work.|Tony Gilroy|<ref name="Vulture">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vulture.com/article/tony-gilroy-andor-star-wars-rogue-one-interview.html|text='Before Anyone Else Defines It, I'm Going to Define It' ''Andor'' creator Tony Gilroy reflects on five years inside the ''Star Wars'' universe.|author=VanArendonk, Kathryn|date=2025-05-16|work=[[Wikipedia:Vulture (website)|''Vulture'']]|archivedate=20250519093736}}</ref>}}
[[File:MikeQuinn.jpg|thumb|right|300px|alt=A young Mike Quinn holds up a Nien Nunb action figure.|Mike Quinn voiced Dewi Pamular.]]
Dewi Pamular was portrayed by [[Matthew Lyons|Matt Lyons]] and voiced by [[Mike Quinn]] in the television show ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', appearing in the [[Andor Season 1|first season's]] eleventh episode, "[[Daughter of Ferrix]],"<ref name="Andor11" /> which aired on [[November 16]], [[2022]].<ref name="Release dates">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-8-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> The character's name was not spoken in the episode but was listed in the credits.<ref name="Andor11" /> Dewi's design was a reuse of the design for<ref name="Trivia2" /> the character [[Cycyed Ock]]<ref name="ROUVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> from the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|Anthology]] film, ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="RO">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> The character's scene was photographed in Middle Peak Quarry in [[Wikipedia:Wirksworth|Wirksworth]], [[Wikipedia:Derbyshire|Derbyshire]] in the [[Wikipedia:United Kingdom|United Kingdom]].<ref name="Trivia3">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e11-trivia-gallery|text="Daughter of Ferrix" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref>

The scene involving Dewi and Freedi required more production meetings then almost any other in the series in order to establish how, when, and why they were going to shoot it and whether the tone could be as funny as they intended. Executive producer [[Tony Gilroy]] wanted it to be "[[Wikipedia:Sergio Leone|Sergio Leone]] meets the [[Wikipedia:Coen brothers|Coen brothers]]" and loved the final result despite the complexity that went into making it.<ref name="Gilroy">{{SWYouTube|_qP3CnChXgk|Andor Season 1 with Tony Gilroy LIVE &#124; Season 2 Coming April 22 on Disney+}}</ref> Gilroy wrote the brothers' dialogue for the scene, including the alien language elements. He was pleased with the result, considering it his best alien dialogue in the series, but felt that it took a lot of work.<ref name="Vulture" />

